;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; jerrylockard.me — DNS zone, hosted at IONOS
;;
;; jerrylockard.me's nameservers moved from Cloudflare to IONOS on 2026-08-30
;; (confirmed at the registry level, not just a DNS-cache snapshot — Jerry's
;; own domain, registered through IONOS). Manage records directly in the
;; IONOS control panel for this domain; this file is the reference copy, not
;; something IONOS imports automatically the way Cloudflare's import tool did.
;;
;; IONOS auto-provisions a mail package (MX, permissive SPF, real DKIM
;; selectors, autodiscover) for every domain by default. That is the OPPOSITE
;; of what this file specifies below — remove IONOS's auto-added mail records
;; entirely and replace them with the reject-everything ones here instead.
;; Nothing receives mail at @jerrylockard.me on purpose; the published contact
;; is jerry@lockard.me, a separate domain with its own real mailbox at IONOS.
;;
;; The A record and TXT verification record below are project-specific to
;; jerrylockard-site — they came directly off the Firebase console (Hosting ->
;; Add custom domain) on 2026-08-29. If Firebase ever asks for different
;; values, the console wins — update this file to match, not the other way
;; around.
;;
;; Deliberately NOT in this file:
;;
;;   CAA     No CAA record is intentional. An absent CAA means any CA may
;;           issue, which is what Firebase (Google Trust Services) needs.
;;           A restrictive CAA is a common cause of stuck certificates.
;;
;; Last reviewed: 2026-08-30 — DNS moved from Cloudflare to IONOS.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$TTL 300

;; --- the site, on Firebase Hosting (project: jerrylockard-site) ----------
;; Apex must be an A record: a CNAME cannot coexist with other records at the
;; zone root.
jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	A	199.36.158.100

;; Firebase's domain-ownership check for this site. Not a one-time proof —
;; Firebase keeps validating the domain/site association against this record,
;; so it stays, not just until the cert issues.
jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	TXT	"hosting-site=jerrylockard-site"

;; www points at the apex. Add www.jerrylockard.me as a custom domain in the
;; Firebase console too, or it answers that Host with nothing configured —
;; then let Firebase redirect www to the apex (it offers this during setup).
www.jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	CNAME	jerrylockard.me.

;; --- mail: this domain sends and receives nothing ------------------------
;; SPF with -all and no senders: any message claiming to be from
;; @jerrylockard.me fails authentication outright.
jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	TXT	"v=spf1 -all"

;; DKIM wildcard with an empty key: no selector can ever validate a signature.
*._domainkey.jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	TXT	"v=DKIM1; p="

;; DMARC set to reject, applied to subdomains as well. No rua= on purpose:
;; sending reports to an address at another domain (lockard.me) needs an
;; authorisation record published in THAT zone first — at IONOS, not here — and
;; a broken rua is worse than none.
_dmarc.jerrylockard.me.	300	IN	TXT	"v=DMARC1; p=reject; sp=reject; adkim=s; aspf=s"
